      "text": "\n\n<think>\nThe user wants me to write an incident retrospective for a production API outage caused by a bad cache invalidation rule. Let me structure this carefully with all the requested sections: impact, timeline, contributing factors, detection gaps, remediation, prevention work, and owner handoff. It should be 450-550 words, practical language for engineers and managers, concise but complete.\n\nLet me think about what makes a good incident retrospective:\n- Blameless tone\n- Specific but not overly technical jargon\n- Clear timeline\n- Actionable items with owners\n- Honest about what went wrong\n- Practical language - not corporate fluff\n\nLet me draft this:\n\nStructure:\n- Header with metadata (date, severity, duration, service)\n- Impact\n- Timeline\n- Contributing Factors\n- Detection Gaps\n- Remediation (what we did to fix it)\n- Prevention (what we're doing to prevent recurrence)\n- Owner Handoff (who owns what going forward)\n\nLet me aim for around 500 words and keep it tight. Let me write it out and count.\n\nLet me draft:\n\n---\n\n**Incident Retrospective: API Outage \u2013 Bad Cache Invalidation Rule**\n**Date:** 2025-06-12 | **Severity:** SEV-1 | **Duration:** 47 min | **Service:** `api-gateway` / `product-catalog`\n\n**Impact**\nBetween 14:02 and 14:49 UTC, the product-catalog API returned 503s for ~92% of read traffic. Downstream effects: storefront checkout page showed stale or missing product data for ~1.2M sessions; search results degraded to a fallback \"results unavailable\" state. No data loss. No PII exposure. Revenue impact estimated at $38K in lost transactions (Finance to confirm).\n\n**Timeline (UTC)**\n- 13:58 \u2013 Deploy `cache-invalidator v2.3.1` to prod via canary (10% traffic). Canary passed.\n- 14:02 \u2013 Full rollout completes. Invalidation rule `PURGE * /products/*` fires on every cache tier simultaneously.\n- 14:04 \u2013 PagerDuty fires: 5xx rate > 5% on `api-gateway`. On-call (J. Oka",
      "text_preview": "\n\n<think>\nThe user wants me to write an incident retrospective for a production API outage caused by a bad cache invalidation rule. Let me structure this carefully with all the requested sections: impact, timeline, contributing factors, detection gaps, remediation, prevention work, and owner handoff. It should be 450-5",
